  "interpretation": "With both targets running concurrently at 2,000 RPS each, pure BAML reached its allocator plateau within the first minute: its post-GC RSS changed 0.047 MiB from 60 seconds to the end and fit 0.020 MiB/min. Python BAML continued upward but decelerated: its fitted post-GC slope fell from 2.161 MiB/min after 30 seconds to 1.739 after 60 seconds, 1.314 after 90 seconds, and 0.187 over the final 30 seconds. Python ended at 95.609 MiB after reaching 95.719 MiB, so this run does not show unbounded linear growth; it is consistent with a slower, stepwise allocator or cache plateau. A longer run or allocation tracing is required to distinguish that from a slow leak."
